Datasets
--------
Amazon MASSIVE 1.1 (en-US, hi-IN) - Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
  FitzGerald et al., "MASSIVE: A 1M-Example Multilingual Natural Language Understanding Dataset", 2022.
  https://github.com/alexa/massive
  Used to train the command (intent + slot) model. Roman-Hindi variants are derived from it by
  rule-based transliteration (indic_transliteration, MIT) and chat-style respelling.

Google FLEURS (hi_in) - Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
  Conneau et al., "FLEURS: Few-shot Learning Evaluation of Universal Representations of Speech", 2022.
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/google/fleurs
  Used only to evaluate speech recognition (not trained on, not shipped).

Models
------
intfloat/multilingual-e5-small - MIT License
  Wang et al., "Multilingual E5 Text Embeddings", 2024. Base encoder of the command model.

DataoceanAI Dolphin (base CTC) - Apache License 2.0
  Meng et al., "Dolphin: A Large-Scale Automatic Speech Recognition Model for Eastern Languages", 2025.
  https://github.com/DataoceanAI/Dolphin  (int8 ONNX export from the sherpa-onnx project)
  Pebble's Hindi/Hinglish speech recognizer.

OpenAI Whisper (base) - MIT License
  Radford et al., "Robust Speech Recognition via Large-Scale Weak Supervision", 2022.
  ONNX exports from the sherpa-onnx project. Pebble's English speech fallback.

Silero VAD - MIT License
  https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad

GTCRN speech enhancement - MIT License (evaluated only, not shipped: it made recognition worse)
  https://github.com/Xiaobin-Rong/gtcrn

